[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29ALet's chart the wayfinder map for your iOS electronics parts tracker. First, we need to pin down the \u001b[1mdestination\u001b[m of\r\n  this map.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mMap Destination\u001b[m: In Wayfinder, a map charts the decisions needed to reach a clear destination (usually a\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  complete V1 specification ready to be broken into implementation tickets, rather than building the whole app inside\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  the map itself). Should the destination of this map be a \u001b[1mlocked V1 product & technical specification\u001b[m for your\u001b[K\r\n  personal iOS electronics parts inventory app—covering the domain model, physical storage organization, part\u001b[K\r\n  lookup/entry workflows, and local storage architecture—ready for implementation?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Yes, the destination is a complete V1 spec for a personal iOS electronics parts tracker, ready to hand off to\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  implementation.\u001b[?7h\u001b[18G\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Great—the destination is locked: \u001b[1ma complete V1 product & technical specification for a personal iOS electronics\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mparts tracker\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Next, let's scan the breadth of the problem space to see where the open decisions and fog lie so we can chart the\r\n  map and its initial frontier tickets. I'll ask one question at a time.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mData Persistence & Multi-Device Sync\u001b[m: Should V1 store your inventory \u001b[1mstrictly locally on-device\u001b[m (e.g.,\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  SQLite/Drift on your iPhone, with manual export/backup), or do you need \u001b[1mcloud sync\u001b[m (e.g., iCloud / CloudKit or a\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  backend like Firebase/Supabase) so it's accessible across multiple devices (like an iPad or Mac)?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Yes, start with local on-device storage (SQLite/Drift) with file export/import for backups, keeping V"]
