[0.100, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\r\n  Great—the destination is locked: \u001b[1ma complete V1 product & technical specification for a personal iOS electronics\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1mparts tracker\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  Next, let's scan the breadth of the problem space to see where the open decisions and fog lie so we can chart the\r\n  map and its initial frontier tickets. I'll ask one question at a time.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mData Persistence & Multi-Device Sync\u001b[m: Should V1 store your inventory \u001b[1mstrictly locally on-device\u001b[m (e.g.,\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\r\n  SQLite/Drift on your iPhone, with manual export/backup), or do you need \u001b[1mcloud sync\u001b[m (e.g., iCloud / CloudKit or a\r\n  backend like Firebase/Supabase) so it's accessible across multiple devices (like an iPad or Mac)?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Yes, start with local on-device storage (SQLite/Drift) with file export/import for backups, keeping V1 offline-\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\r\n  first with zero server/account overhead.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> JSON on device\u001b[m\r\n\n  Got it: \u001b[1mJSON file on device\u001b[m.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mScope of What You're Tracking\u001b[m: At a high level, which of these pillars are \u001b[1min scope for V1\u001b[m versus \u001b[1mout of\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mscope\u001b[m?\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mParts & Quantities\u001b[m: What components you own and how many you have on hand.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mStorage Locations\u001b[m: Where each part physically lives (e.g., cabinet, drawer, grid bin, anti-static bag).\r\n  3. \u001b[1mProjects / BOMs (Bills of Materials)\u001b[m: Allocating or reserving parts for specific electronics projects you're\r\n  building.\r\n  4. \u001b[1mSupplier & Ordering / Low-Stock Alerts\u001b[m: Tracking distributor part numbers (DigiKey, Mouser, LCSC), prices,\r\n  datasheets, and reorder thresholds.\r\n\n  ➡\r\n⣷  \u001b[90mGen\u001b[94merati\u001b[90mng...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use @ to mention files and give the model more context.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────"]
