[0.000, "o", "rarchy Depth\u001b[m: How are your physical parts containers organized at your workbench, and how should the app\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  model them?\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mOption A — Fixed two-level (\u001b[94;22mContainer\u001b[39;1m → \u001b[94;22mSlot\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: You define top-level \u001b[1mContainers\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94m\"SMD Binder #1\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94m\"IC Drawer\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mCabinet\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94m\"Passives Grid Box A\"\u001b[m) and inside them \u001b[1mSlots\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94m\"Page 4, Strip 2\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94m\"Drawer R2C3\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94m\"Cell B4\"\u001b[m). Fast to\r\n  pick in two taps without deep tree navigation.\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B — Arbitrary tree hierarchy\u001b[m: A location can have a parent location to any depth (e.g., \u001b[94mShelf 1 → Cabinet\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mA → Drawer 3 → Sub-compartment B\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption C — Flat labels\u001b[m: Just a single text string or tag per location (e.g., \u001b[94m\"Cabinet A - Drawer 12\"\u001b[m).\r\n\n  ➡\r\n⣯  \u001b[94mL\u001b[90moading...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /model to switch between available models.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m─────────────────────"]
