[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[24A\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mContainer Layout & Slot Addressing\u001b[m: When you create a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m, how should its \u001b[1mSlots\u001b[m be defined and\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption A — Structured Grid Generator + Freeform Slots\u001b[m, because electronics drawers and SMD compartment boxes are\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mMultiple Parts per Slot & Unass\u001b[?7h\u001b[42G\u001b[m\n\n\n\n\n\n\b\b\b\u001b[38;5;214mBlocked\u001b[m · Test jlcpcb.com /api/overseas-pcb-order selectSmtComponentLis...\u001b[90m · 3m24s\u001b[m\r\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[24A  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mContainer Layout & Slot Addressing\u001b[m: When you create a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m, how should its \u001b[1mSlots\u001b[m be defined and\u001b[K\r\n  displayed?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption A — Structured Grid Generator + Freeform Slots\u001b[m: When creating a Container, you can pick either:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[6C1. \u001b[1mGrid Container\u001b[m (specify Rows × Columns, e.g., \u001b[94m4 × 6\u001b[m or \u001b[94mA–D × 1–6\u001b[m), which automatically generates addressable\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mSlots\u001b[m (\u001b[94mA1\u001b[m..\u001b[94mD6\u001b[m) and lets the UI render a visual 2D grid map highlighting which slot holds your part, or\r\n\u001b[6C2. \u001b[1mFreeform / List Container\u001b[m, where Slots are just named labels created on the fly (e.g., \u001b[94m\"Page 1\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94m\"Bag 3\"\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m\"Top Shelf\"\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B — Simple Named Slots Only\u001b[m: Every Slot is just a string label (e.g., \u001b[94m\"A1\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94m\"Drawer 12\"\u001b[m) created on the\r\n  fly when assigning a part, without Container grid dimensions or 2D grid visualizations.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption A — Str"]
[0.000, "o", "uctured Grid Generator + Freeform Slots\u001b[m, because electronics drawers and SMD compartment boxes are\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  almost always 2D grids, and seeing the highlighted cell \u001b[94m(Row B, Col 4)\u001b[m on a visual grid makes finding a part at the\r\n  workbench instant.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> Option B\u001b[m\r\n\n  Got it—keeping it simple with \u001b[1mOption B (Simple Named Slots Only)\u001b[m created on the fly.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mMultiple Parts per Slot & Unassigned Parts\u001b[m**\u001b[?7h\u001b[55G\r\n\n \u001b[33m┃\u001b[m \u001b[94mself\u001b[m needs approval for \u001b[33;1mBash\u001b[m\r\n \u001b[33m┃\u001b[m \u001b[90m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
