[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[27A1. \u001b[1mSharing a Slot\u001b[m: Can multiple distinct \u001b[1mParts\u001b[m live in the same \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m (for example, keeping both \u001b[94m1N4148\u001b[m and \u001b[94m1N4007\u001b[m\r\n  diodes in \u001b[94m\"Box A → Slot D2\"\u001b[m), or is a Slot strictly 1-to-1 with a single Part?\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mUnassigned (\"Loose\") Parts\u001b[m: When a new LCSC order arrives and you enter the parts before putting them away in a\r\n  Container, can a Part have \u001b[1mno Container/Slot assigned yet\u001b[m (so you can filter by \u001b[3m\"Unassigned / Loose\"\u001b[m when you sit\u001b[K\r\n  down to sort them)?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes to both\u001b[m: multiple Parts can share the same \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m, and both \u001b[94mcontainer\u001b[m and \u001b[94mslot\u001b[m on a Part are\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  optional so newly arrived or loose parts can be tracked before they are put away.\u001b[?7h\u001b[84G\r\n\u001b[K\n  Got it: \u001b[1mstrictly 1 Part per Slot\u001b[m! Let's make sure the edge cases around that 1-to-1 rule and unassigned parts are\r\n  crystal clear:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mEnforcing 1-Part-per-"]
[0.000, "o", "Slot & Unassigned Parts\u001b[m:\u001b[?7h\u001b[56G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7h\u001b[1G\n  1. Since a \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m holds at most one \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m, what happens if you assign a Part to a \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m that is already\r\n  occupied by another Part? Should the UI prevent selecting occupied slots by default (or offer to \u001b[1mswap / evict\u001b[m the\r\n  existing part to \"Unassigned\")?\u001b[K\r\n  2. What if a Part is placed in a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m \u001b[3mwithout\u001b[m specifying a \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m (or has \u001b[1mno Container at all\u001b[m because it just\r\n  arrived in the mail)—are multiple unassigned/slotless parts allowed, with the 1-to-1 uniqueness enforced\u001b[K\r\n  specifically when a \u001b[94mSlot\u001b[m is named (\u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m pair is unique)?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes\u001b[m: \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m is strictly unique (1 Part per Slot; the picker shows which slots are already taken and\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  warns/prevents double-assigning), while Parts without a Slot (either unassigned to any Container, or placed in a\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  Conta\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\u001b[5D\u001b[?202"]
