[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A  Got it: \u001b[1mstrictly 1 Part per Slot\u001b[m! Let's make sure the edge cases around that 1-to-1 rule and unassigned parts are\u001b[K\r\n  crystal clear:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mEnforcing 1-Part-per-Slot & Unassigned Parts\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  1. Since a \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m holds at most one \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m, what happens if you assign a Part to a \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m that is already\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  occupied by another Part? Should the UI prevent selecting occupied slots by default (or offer to \u001b[1mswap / evict\u001b[m the\r\n  existing part to \"Unassigned\")?\r\n  2. What if a Part is placed in a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m \u001b[3mwithout\u001b[m specifying a \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m (or has \u001b[1mno Container at all\u001b[m because it just\r\n  arrived in the mail)—are multiple unassigned/slotless parts allowed, with the 1-to-1 uniqueness enforced\r\n  specifically when a \u001b[94mSlot\u001b[m is named (\u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m pair is unique)?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes\u001b[m: \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m is strictly unique (1 Part per Slot; the picker shows which slots are "]
[0.000, "o", "already taken and\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  warns/prevents double-assigning), while Parts without a Slot (either unassigned to any Container, or placed in a\r\n  Container with no Slot specified) don't conflict with each other.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mContainer Lifecycle (First-Class Entity vs. String Tag)\u001b[m: Should a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m be a managed entity in the JSON\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  store (with an \u001b[94mid\u001b[m, \u001b[94mname\u001b[m, and optional \u001b[94mdescription\u001b[m, so you can rename \u001b[94m\"Drawer Cabinet 1\"\u001b[m in one place and browse\r\n  empty containers), while a \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m is a simple string label (e.g., \u001b[94m\"A1\"\u001b[m) on the Part within that Container?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes\u001b[m:\u001b[?7h\u001b[10G\r\n\n \u001b[33m┃\u001b[m \u001b[94mself\u001b[m needs approval for \u001b[33;1mBash\u001b[m\r\n \u001b[33m┃\u001b[m \u001b[90m────────────────"]
