[0.516, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[27A\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7h\u001b[1G\n\u001b[37;1m/Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/.scratch/parts-tracker-v1/issues/03-storage-location-h\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 1 \u001b[m    Type: grilling\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 2 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39mStatus: claimed\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 2 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39mStatus: resolved\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 3 \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 4 \u001b[m    ## Question\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 5 \u001b[?7h\u001b[6G\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m   \u001b[94m @@ 2 lines hidden @@\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 8 \u001b[m    Key decisions to resolve:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 9 \u001b[m    1. **Hierarchy model**: Flat labels (e.g., \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`\"Cabinet A - R3C4"]
[0.000, "o", "\"`\u001b[m), fixed 2-level (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Container → Slot`\u001b[m), or\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[37m         arbitrary nesting (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Room/Shelf → Cabinet → Drawer → Compartment`\u001b[m)?\u001b[?7h\u001b[76G\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m10 \u001b[m    2. **Grid / coordinate addressing**: Do you want first-class support for grid coordinates (e.g., rows \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`A–F`\u001b[m ×\r\n\t\u001b[37m\u001b[1K columns \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`1–8`\u001b[m, or numbered binder pages/strips) for visual bin-finding, or simple named locations?\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m11 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m3. **Location lifecycle**: Moving parts between locations, viewing everything inside a container/drawer, and\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39mhandling unlocated (\"loose / to-be-sorted\") parts.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m11 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m3. **Location lifecycle**: Moving parts between locations, viewing everything inside a container/drawer, and\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mhandling unlocated (\"loose / to-be-sorted\") parts.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r"]
[0.001, "o", "\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m12 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m13 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m## Answer\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m14 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m15 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m1. **Fixed two-level hierarchy (`Container` → `Slot`)**:\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m  … 8 more lines (f for full diff)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1mshift+tab\u001b[90;22m to auto-approve file edits\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mAccept this file edit?\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[C\u001b[94m 1. Yes, accept this change\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. No, reject this change\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mf\u001b[90;22m full diff\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
[4.646, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[30A\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes\u001b[m: \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m is strictly unique (1 Part per Slot; the picker shows which slots are already taken and\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  warns/prevents double-assigning), while Parts without a Slot (either unassigned to any Container, or placed in a\u001b[K\r\n  Container with no Slot specified) don't conflict with each other.\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mContainer Lifecycle (First-Class Entity vs. String Tag)\u001b[m: Should a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m be a managed entity in the JSON\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  store (with an \u001b[94mid\u001b[m, \u001b[94mname\u001b[m, and optional \u001b[94mdescription\u001b[m, so you can rename \u001b[94m\"Drawer Cabinet 1\"\u001b[m in one place and browse\r\n  empty containers), while a \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m is a simple string label (e.g., \u001b[94m\"A1\"\u001b[m) on the Part within that Container?\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b"]
