[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes\u001b[m: \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m is strictly unique (1 Part per Slot; the picker shows which slots are already taken and\u001b[K\r\n  warns/prevents double-assigning), while Parts without a Slot (either unassigned to any Container, or placed in a\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  Container with no Slot specified) don't conflict with each other.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mContainer Lifecycle (First-Class Entity vs. String Tag)\u001b[m: Should a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m be a managed entity in the JSON\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  store (with an \u001b[94mid\u001b[m, \u001b[94mname\u001b[m, and optional \u001b[94mdescription\u001b[m, so you can rename \u001b[94m\"Drawer Cabinet 1\"\u001b[m in one place and browse\r\n  empty containers), while a \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m is a simple string label (e.g., \u001b[94m\"A1\"\u001b[m) on the Part within that Container?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes\u001b[m: \u001b[1mCo"]
[0.000, "o", "ntainers\u001b[m are first-class entities (\u001b[94mid\u001b[m, \u001b[94mname\u001b[m, optional \u001b[94mdescription\u001b[m) so they can be listed, created, or\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\r\n  renamed cleanly, whereas a \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m is a lightweight string label on the Part (unique per \u001b[94m(containerId, slot)\u001b[m when \u001b[94mslot\u001b[m\r\n  is non-null).\r\n\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(map.md)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEdited\u001b[m 3 files \u001b[37m(GLOSSARY.md, 03-storage-location-hierarchy.md, map.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n  We have resolved \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk3f51b8b10e1cd51b;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/.scratch/parts-tracker-v1/issues/03-storage-location-hierarchy.md\u0007Physical storage location hierarchy and addressing\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and updated both \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk7874b5d2a47186a5;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and\r\n  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkf616f52e63e7e3f3;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/.scratch/parts-tr"]
