[0.000, "o", "rs\"\u001b[m) and a list of parameter key-value pairs (\u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m, e.g., \u001b[94mCapacitance:\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94m\"100nF\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94mVoltage Rated: \"50V\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94mTolerance: \"±10%\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94mTemperature Coefficient: \"X7R\"\u001b[m).\r\n\n  How should categories and electrical specs be modeled on a \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m?\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mOption A (Flexible key-value specs + string category)\u001b[m: Store \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m as an optional string (auto-filled from\r\n  LCSC's \u001b[94mcatalogName\u001b[m, with quick-pick suggestions from categories already in your catalog) and \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m as an ordered\r\n  \u001b[94mMap<String, String>\u001b[m of parameter names to values (auto-populated from LCSC's \u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m with \u001b[94m\"-\"\u001b[m placeholders\r\n  stripped, and freely editable as key-value rows in the UI).\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B (Fixed per-category schemas)\u001b[m: Define rigid types (Resistor, Capacitor, IC, etc.) with dedicated typed\r\n  fields per category.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes to Option A — store \u001b[94;22mcategory\u001b[39;1m as a string and \u001b[94;22mspecs\u001b[39;1m as an o"]
[0.000, "o", "rdered \u001b[94;22mMap<String, String>\u001b[39;1m populated from LCSC's\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[39;1m and editable as key-value pairs.\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> option A\u001b[m\r\n⣯  \u001b[90mLoading...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
