[0.034, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K  • \u001b[94mname\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mproductDescEn\u001b[m (falling back to \u001b[94mproductIntroEn\u001b[m or \u001b[94mproductModel\u001b[m)\u001b[?7h\u001b[74G\r\n  • \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mproductModel\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mmanufacturer\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mbrandNameEn\u001b[m\n\u001b[26D\u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mcatalogName\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94m\"Ceramic Capacitors\"\u001b[m)\u001b[K\n\u001b[51D\u001b[94mpackage\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mencapStandard\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94m\"0603\"\u001b[m)\n\u001b[38D\u001b[94mdatasheetUrl\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mpdfUrl\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[21D\u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m ← \u001b[94m{ paramNameEn: paramValueEn }\u001b[m from \u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m (skipping \u001b[94m\"-\"\u001b[m placeholders)\r\n\u001b[K\n  Once fetched into the form, every field remains a normal local field that you can freely edit or override before\r\n  saving, and is persisted locally in JSON.\u001b[K\r\n\n  How should we handle \u001b[1mduplicate \u001b[94;22mlcscCode\u001b[m if you enter a \u001b[94mCx\u001b[5b\u001b[m that's already in your catalog?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mOption A (Warn, don't hard-block)\u001b[m: Show an inline warning linking to the existing Part (so you can jump to it and\r\n  increment its quantity instead"]
[0.001, "o", " of accidentally creating a duplicate), but still allow saving if you intentionally\r\n  want a second entry (e.g., overflow stock in another container).\n\u001b[55D\u001b[1mB (Strict uniqueness)\u001b[m: Disallow saving two Parts with the same \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes to the LCSC field mapping above and Option A (warn with a quick link to the existing Part when \u001b[94;22mlcscCode\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1malready exists, without hard-blocking).\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[?7h\u001b[61G\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> A\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThinking...\u001b[m \u001b[37m(The \"Not yet specified\" section of `map.md` highlights the need to address search normalization for...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[33m○\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mUsing\u001b[m ReadFile \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\n\u001b[20D\u001b[90m \u001b[94mspeci\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[19D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mLCSC auto-fill mapping, manual overrides, and duplicate \u001b[m\u001b[94mCxxxxxx\u001b[m\u001b[1m handling\u001b[m: When you enter a \u001b[94mCxxxxxx\u001b[m code in\u001b[K\r\n  the Add/Edit Part form and tap \"Fetch from LCSC\", here is the proposed mapping from the LCSC detail payload:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  • \u001b[94mname\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mproductDescEn\u001b[m (falling back to \u001b[94mproductIntroEn\u001b[m or \u001b[94mproductModel\u001b[m)\r\n  • \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mproductModel\u001b[m\r\n  • \u001b[94mmanufacturer\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mbrandNameEn\u001b[m\r\n  • \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mcatalogName\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94m\"Ceramic Capacitors\"\u001b[m)\r\n  • \u001b[94mpackage\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mencapStandard\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94m\"0603\"\u001b[m)\r\n  • \u001b[94mdatasheetUrl\u001b[m ← \u001b[94mpdfUrl\u001b[m\r\n  • \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m ← \u001b[94m{ paramNameEn: paramValueEn }\u001b[m from \u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m (skipping \u001b[94m\"-\"\u001b[m placeholders)\r\n\n  Once fetched into the form, every field remains a normal local field that you can freely edit or override before\r\n  saving, and is persisted locally in JSON.\r\n\n  How should we handle \u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "1mduplicate \u001b[94;22mlcscCode\u001b[m if you enter a \u001b[94mCx\u001b[5b\u001b[m that's already in your catalog?\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mOption A (Warn, don't hard-block)\u001b[m: Show an inline warning linking to the existing Part (so you can jump to it and\r\n  increment its quantity instead of accidentally creating a duplicate), but still allow saving if you intentionally\r\n  want a second entry (e.g., overflow stock in another container).\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B (Strict uniqueness)\u001b[m: Disallow saving two Parts with the same \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes to the LCSC field mapping above and Option A (warn with a quick link to the existing Part when \u001b[94;22mlcscCode\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1malready exists, without hard-blocking).\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> A\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 20.2s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(I'm thinking through how to approach this.)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m"]
