[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29AThe design tree for \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk7e858995835eb2a1;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/.scratch/parts-tracker-v1/issues/02-part-domain-model-and-specs.md\u0007Part domain model, categories, and electrical specifications\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 is now complete:\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mIdentity & Core Fields\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[1mRequired\u001b[m: \u001b[94mid\u001b[m (UUID), \u001b[94mname\u001b[m (display title), \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m (integer ≥ 0, default \u001b[94m0\u001b[m).\r\n\t\u001b[1mOptional catalog & supplier fields\u001b[m: \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m (normalized uppercase \u001b[94mCx\u001b[5b\u001b[m), \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmanufacturer\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mpackage\u001b[m (footprint/case, e.g., \u001b[94m\"0603\"\u001b[m, \u001b[94m\"DIP-8\"\u001b[m), \u001b[94mdatasheetUrl\u001b[m, \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m (ordered \u001b[94mMap<String, String>\u001b[m).\u001b[K\n\u001b[99D• \u001b[1mOptional workbench & inventory fields\u001b[m: \u001b[94mcontainerId\u001b[m, \u001b[94mslot\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlowStockThreshold\u001b[m (integer threshold where \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m<= lowStockThreshold\u001b[m flags low stock), \u001b[94mnotes\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mCategories &"]
[0.000, "o", " Electrical Specifications\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m is an optional string (auto-filled from LCSC's \u001b[94mcatalogName\u001b[m, with quick-pick suggestions from\r\n\u001b[6Ccategories already in the catalog).\u001b[K\n\u001b[35D• \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m is an ordered key-value map (\u001b[94mMap<String, String>\u001b[m) of parameter names to values (e.g., \u001b[94m{\"Capacitance\":\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m\"100nF\", \"Voltage Rated\": \"50V\"}\u001b[m), auto-populated from LCSC's \u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m and freely editable as key-value rows\r\n\u001b[6Cin the UI.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mLCSC Auto-Fill & Duplicate Handling\u001b[m:\r\n      • Fetching a \u001b[94mCx\u001b[5b\u001b[m code pre-fills \u001b[94mname\u001b[m (\u001b[94mproductDescEn ?? productIntroEn ?? productModel\u001b[m), \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m (\u001b[94mproductModel\u001b[m),\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mmanufacturer\u001b[m (\u001b[94mbrandNameEn\u001b[m), \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m (\u001b[94mcatalogName\u001b[m), \u001b[94mpackage\u001b[m (\u001b[94mencapStandard\u001b[m), \u001b[94mdatasheetUrl\u001b[m (\u001b[94mpdfUrl\u001b[m), and \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C(\u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m excluding \u001b[94m\"-\"\u001b[m placeholders) into the form as normal editable local fields.\u001b[K\n\u001b[87D• Ent"]
[0.000, "o", "ering a duplicate \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m warns with a quick link to the existing \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m (to easily update its stock),\r\n\u001b[6Cwithout hard-blocking if a second catalog entry is intentional.\u001b[K\r\n  4. \u001b[1mStock & Location Cardinality\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • Each \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m has a single \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m and lives in at most one \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m location (\u001b[94mcontainerId?\u001b[m, \u001b[94mslot?\u001b[m).\r\n\u001b[K\n\n  Does this capture our shared understanding so I can resolve [Part domain model, categories, and electrical\r\n  specificatio\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\u001b[12D\u001b[?2026l"]
