[0.000, "o", "ntainers\u001b[m (array of \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m objects), and \u001b[94mparts\u001b[m (array of \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m objects) — using \u001b[94mcontainers\u001b[m rather than \u001b[94mlocations\u001b[m\r\n  to match \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd38be6d1e566237b;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mIdentical live & backup format\u001b[m: The live \u001b[94mparts_catalog.json\u001b[m file and exported backup files use the exact same\r\n  JSON envelope, so copying \u001b[94mparts_catalog.json\u001b[m directly out of the iOS Files app is indistinguishable from an\r\n  exported backup.\r\n  3. \u001b[1mVersion handling\u001b[m: On load/import, if \u001b[94mschemaVersion > 1\u001b[m, reject with a clear error message rather than silently\r\n  corrupting newer data; if \u001b[94mparts_catalog.json\u001b[m does not exist yet on first launch, initialize an empty v1 catalog\r\n  (\u001b[94mcontainers: []\u001b[m, \u001b[94mparts: []\u001b[m).\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes — adopt this exact \u001b[94;22mschemaVersion: 1\u001b[39;1m envelope\u001b[m using \u001b[94mcontainers\u001b[m and \u001b[94mparts\u001b[m, identi"]
[0.000, "o", "cal format for live storage\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  and exported backups, and strict \u001b[94mschemaVersion\u001b[m check on load/import.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[m\r\n⣟  \u001b[90mGener\u001b[94mating\u001b[90m...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
