[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mImport Semantics, Safety Backup, and Referential Integrity Validation\u001b[m: When importing a JSON catalog file\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk954dbd703895d5fa;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ **Yes — use validated full-snapshot replace with a confirmation summary, automatic \u001b[94mparts_catalog.backup.json\u001b[m **\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\r\n\n\n\n\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mImport Semantics, Safety Backup, and Referential Integrity Validation\u001b[m: When importing a JSON catalog file\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  (or when a user deletes a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m or edits the JSON externally), how should conflicts and invariants be handled?\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mFull Snapshot Replace with Confirmation Summary (No Complex Merge)\u001b[m:\n\u001b[66D• Because this is a single-user personal catalog where backups or desktop scripts represent whole-catalog\r\n\u001b[6Csnapshots, importing a JSON file \u001b[1mreplaces\u001b[m the current catalog rather than attempting a multi-key merge.\r\n\u001b[6C• Before replacing, the app validates the chosen file and shows a confirmation dialog summarizing the incoming\r\n\u001b[6Cfile (\u001b[94m\"Replace current catalog (X parts, Y containers) with backup from <updatedAt> (A parts, B containers)?\"\u001b[m).\r\n\u001b[6C• Right before overwriting \u001b[94mparts_catalog.json\u001b[m, the app copies the existing \u001b[94mparts_catalog.json\u001b[m to \u001b[94mparts_catalog.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mbackup.json\u001b[m in the Documents dire"]
[0.000, "o", "ctory so an accidental import or external file corruption can always be\r\n\u001b[6Crecovered.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mStrict Import Validation (All-or-Nothing)\u001b[m:\n\u001b[41D• Reject the import (leaving the live catalog untouched) with a clear error message if:\r\n\t  • The file is malformed JSON or \u001b[94mschemaVersion\u001b[m is unsupported (\u001b[94m!= 1\u001b[m).\r\n\t  • Any \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m or \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m is missing required fields (\u001b[94mid\u001b[m, \u001b[94mname\u001b[m, or \u001b[94mquantity < 0\u001b[m) or has duplicate \u001b[94mid\u001b[ms.\r\n\t  • Two \u001b[1mParts\u001b[m claim the same non-empty \u001b[94m(containerId, slot)\u001b[m pair (violating the 1-to-1 \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m rule in\r\n\t  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jke8224542cba62ad3;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007).\r\n\t  • Any \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m references a \u001b[94mcontainerId\u001b[m that does not exist in \u001b[94mcontainers\u001b[m.\r\n\n  3. \u001b[1mContainer Deletion Referential Integrity\u001b[m:\n\u001b[40D• When deleting a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m in the app's Manage Containers sheet, any \u001b[1mParts\u001b[m currently in that "]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m are\r\n\u001b[6Cunassigned (\u001b[94mcontainerId: null, slot: null\u001b[m) in the same atomic save so no dangling \u001b[94mcontainerId\u001b[m can ever be\r\n\u001b[6Cwritten.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes — use validated full-snapshot replace with a confirmation summary, automatic \u001b[94;22mparts_catalog.backup.json\u001b[39;1m pre-\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mimport b\u001b[m\r\n⣷  \u001b[90mWorking...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: When reviewing a file edit, press f to see the full diff.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
