[0.000, "o", "h/parts-tracker-v1/issues/06-search-and-unit-normalization.md\u0007Catalog search, filtering, and engineering unit normalization\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007**.\r\n\n  Here is Round 1 to resolve the decisions for this ticket:\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mEngineering Unit & Shorthand Equivalence\u001b[m: When searching across a \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m's \u001b[94mname\u001b[m and \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m (from \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk50c465c78c327f3a;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007),\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  how far should unit normalization go?\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mOption A (Canonical SI + R-notation normalization + Unicode folding)\u001b[m: Normalize both indexed part text (\u001b[94mname\u001b[m,\r\n  \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m values) and query tokens in two ways:\n\u001b[39D1. \u001b[1mText folding\u001b[m: Case-insensitive matching with Unicode symbol folding (\u001b[94mµ\u001b[m/\u001b[94mμ\u001b[m → \u001b[94mu\u001b[m, \u001b[94mΩ\u001b[m/\u001b[94mohm\u001b[m/\u001b[94mohms\u001b[m → \u001b[94mr\u001b[m, stripping \u001b[94m±\u001b[m).\r\n\u001b[6C2. \u001b[1mCanonical engineering value matching\u001b[m: Parse explicitly unit/pr"]
[0.000, "o", "efix-marked tokens—both standard SI (\u001b[94m4.7k\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m7kΩ\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4700R\u001b[m, \u001b[94m100mΩ\u001b[m, \u001b[94m0.1uF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m10\u001b[4bpF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4.7uH\u001b[m, \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m) and EE infix shorthand (\u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m, \u001b[94m100r\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4r7\u001b[m, \u001b[94m3v3\u001b[m, \u001b[94m2n2\u001b[m)—into\r\n\u001b[6Ccanonical \u001b[94m(Dimension, baseValue)\u001b[m pairs (Resistance in Ω, Capacitance in F, Inductance in H, Voltage in V,\r\n\u001b[6CCurrent in A, Power in W, Frequency in Hz) compared within floating-point tolerance (10⁻⁶ relative). Do \u001b[1mnot\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cexpand bare 3-digit EIA numbers like \u001b[94m104\u001b[m into \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m/\u001b[94m100kΩ\u001b[m (avoiding false positives against \u001b[94mCx\u001b[5b\u001b[m codes and\r\n\u001b[6Cquantities;\r\n\n⣷  \u001b[94mGene\u001b[90mrating...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /diff to view uncommitted changes in your workspace.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
