[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption A\u001b[m: Canonical SI + EE infix shorthand (\u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m4700R\u001b[m, \u001b[94m0.1uF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m3v3\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m) plus Unicode\u001b[K\r\n  folding (\u001b[94mµ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mu\u001b[m, \u001b[94mΩ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mr\u001b[m/\u001b[94mohm\u001b[m), while leaving bare 3-digit codes (\u001b[94m104\u001b[m) to normal substring matching against \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m/\u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mMulti-Token Query Semantics, Searchable Fields, and Ordering\u001b[m: In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkccb8bf7628dc6c25;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/lib/prototype_workbench.dart#L1796-L1806\u0007VariantBDarkCommandAccordion._filtered\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007,\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  the prototype matched the entire query as a single contiguous substring (\u001b[94mhay.contains(q)\u001b[m), which fails when tokens\r\n  are typed in a different order (e.g., \u001b[94m\"0603 100nF X7R\"\u001b[m). How should multi-token search and ordering work?\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mSearchable fields\u001b[m: Match against \u001b[9"]
