[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\r\n  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption A\u001b[m: Keep the single-row chip bar (\u001b[94mBy Container\u001b[m toggle + \u001b[94mAll\u001b[m / \u001b[94mLow Stock\u001b[m / \u001b[94mUnassigned\u001b[m / dynamic \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  chips) combined via \u001b[1mAND\u001b[m with the search omnibox, hiding containers with zero matching parts in \u001b[94mBy Container\u001b[m mode\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  when a filter or search query is active.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> please ask questions one at a time\u001b[m\r\n\n  Sorry about that—let's go one at a time.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mEngineering Unit & Shorthand Equivalence\u001b[m: When searching across a \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m's \u001b[94mname\u001b[m and \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m (from \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk1f85aa3d359a6ba8;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007),\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  how far should unit normalization go?\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mOption "]
[0.000, "o", "A (Canonical SI + EE infix shorthand + Unicode folding)\u001b[m:\n\u001b[61D1. \u001b[1mText folding\u001b[m: Case-insensitive matching with Unicode symbol folding (\u001b[94mµ\u001b[m/\u001b[94mμ\u001b[m → \u001b[94mu\u001b[m, \u001b[94mΩ\u001b[m/\u001b[94mohm\u001b[m/\u001b[94mohms\u001b[m → \u001b[94mr\u001b[m, stripping \u001b[94m±\u001b[m).\r\n\u001b[6C2. \u001b[1mCanonical engineering value matching\u001b[m: Parse explicitly unit/prefix-marked tokens—both standard SI (\u001b[94m4.7k\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m7kΩ\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4700R\u001b[m, \u001b[94m100mΩ\u001b[m, \u001b[94m0.1uF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m10\u001b[4bpF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4.7uH\u001b[m, \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m) and EE infix shorthand (\u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m, \u001b[94m100r\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4r7\u001b[m, \u001b[94m3v3\u001b[m, \u001b[94m2n2\u001b[m)—into\r\n\u001b[6Ccanonical \u001b[94m(Dimension, baseValue)\u001b[m pairs so \u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m4700R\u001b[m and \u001b[94m0.1uF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m match across \u001b[94mname\u001b[m and \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m.\r\n\u001b[6CLeave bare 3-digit EIA numbers like \u001b[94m104\u001b[m to normal substring matching against \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m/\u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m (avoiding false\r\n\u001b[6Cpositives against \u001b[94mCx\u001b[5b\u001b[m codes and quantities).\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B (In"]
[0.000, "o", "clude 3-digit EIA code expansion)\u001b[m: Everything in Option A, plus expanding bare 3-digit numbers like\r\n  \u001b[94m104\u001b[m or \u001b[94m472\u001b[m into equivalent capacitance/resistance values (\u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m / \u001b[94m100kΩ\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4.7nF\u001b[m / \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption C (Substring + Unicode folding only)\u001b[m: Only fold \u001b[94mµ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mu\u001b[m and \u001b[94mΩ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mr\u001b[m/\u001b[94mohm\u001b[m without cross-unit numeric equivalence (\u001b[94m0.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94m1uF\u001b[m would not match \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m, and \u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m would not match \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m).\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption A\u001b[m (Canonical SI + EE infix shorthand + Unicode folding, without bare 3-digit EIA expansion). Does that\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  work for you?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> A\u001b[m\r\n⣾  \u001b[90mLoadin\u001b[94mg...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────"]
[0.001, "o", "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[84X\u001b[84C\u001b[2mGemini 4 Argon · medium\u001b[m\r\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
