[0.000, "o", "pecification:\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mState Management (\u001b[94;22mChangeNotifier\u001b[39;1m vs. External Framework)\u001b[m: For a single-workbench-screen catalog where the\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  entire dataset fits comfortably in memory alongside an on-device JSON file, how should reactive UI state be\r\n  managed?\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mOption A (Built-in Flutter \u001b[94;22mChangeNotifier\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mListenableBuilder\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: A single deep \u001b[94mCatalogStore extends ChangeNotifier\u001b[m\r\n  module holds the live \u001b[94mcontainers\u001b[m and \u001b[94mparts\u001b[m state, enforces domain invariants, and notifies listeners on\r\n  mutations—requiring zero third-party state management packages or code generation.\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B (\u001b[94;22mflutter_riverpod\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: Manage state via Riverpod \u001b[94mNotifierProvider\u001b[m / \u001b[94mAsyncNotifierProvider\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption C (\u001b[94;22mflutter_bloc\u001b[39;1m / \u001b[94;22mprovider\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: Use Bloc cubits or \u001b[94mpackage:provider\u001b[m.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommend Option A (Built-in \u001b[94;22mChangeNotifier\u001b"]
