[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29AHere is the grilling round to settle the architecture, module seams, and dependencies before locking the V1\r\n  specification:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mState Management (\u001b[94;22mChangeNotifier\u001b[39;1m vs. External Framework)\u001b[m: For a single-workbench-screen catalog where the\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  entire dataset fits comfortably in memory alongside an on-device JSON file, how should reactive UI state be\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\r\n  managed?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mOption A (Built-in Flutter \u001b[94;22mChangeNotifier\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mListenableBuilder\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: A single deep \u001b[94mCatalogStore extends ChangeNotifier\u001b[m\r\n  module holds the live \u001b[94mcontainers\u001b[m and \u001b[94mparts\u001b[m state, enforces domain invariants, and notifies listeners on\u001b[K\r\n  mutations—requiring zero third-party state management packages or code generation.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B (\u001b[94;22mflutter_riverpod\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: Manage state via Riverpod \u001b[94mNotifierProvider\u001b[m / \u001b[94mAsyncNotifierProvider\u001b[m.\n\u001b[89D\u001b[1mC (\u001b[94;22mflutter_bloc\u001b[39;1"]
