[0.033, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29A• \u001b[1mOption A (Built-in Flutter \u001b[94;22mChangeNotifier\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mListenableBuilder\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: A single deep \u001b[94mCatalogStore extends ChangeNotifier\u001b[m\r\n  module holds the live \u001b[94mcontainers\u001b[m and \u001b[94mparts\u001b[m state, enforces domain invariants, and notifies listeners on\u001b[K\r\n  mutations—requiring zero third-party state management packages or code generation.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B (\u001b[94;22mflutter_riverpod\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: Manage state via Riverpod \u001b[94mNotifierProvider\u001b[m / \u001b[94mAsyncNotifierProvider\u001b[m.\n\u001b[89D\u001b[1mC (\u001b[94;22mflutter_bloc\u001b[39;1m / \u001b[94;22mprovider\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: Use Bloc cubits or \u001b[94mpackage:provider\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommend Option A (Built-in \u001b[94;22mChangeNotifier\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mListenableBuilder\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: It matches the single-screen architecture\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  prototyped in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkc319eb9258426b86;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/.scratch/parts-tracker-v1/issues/04-workbench-ui-prototype.md"]
[0.000, "o", "\u0007Workbench UI flow and visual prototype\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, keeps dependency overhead at zero, and concentrates all\u001b[?7h\u001b[112G\r\n  catalog mutations and domain invariants inside one cohesive module.\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mDeep Module Seams & Adapters\u001b[m: Following \u001b[94mcodebase-design\u001b[m, we want a few deep modules with small interfaces\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  placed at real seams (where production and test adapters actually vary) rather than shallow pass-through layers.\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  Should we structure \u001b[94mlib/\u001b[m around these three module seams?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[94mCatalogStore\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mCatalogPersistence\u001b[39;1m seam\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[94mCatalogStore\u001b[m (deep module) owns all domain rules: 1-to-1 \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m uniqueness, duplicate \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cwarning lookup, stock clamping (\u001b[94m>= 0\u001b[m), container deletion cascading (\u001b[94mcontainerId: null, slot: null\u001b[m), and pre-\r\n\u001b[6Cimport validation.\u001b[K\n\u001b[18D• \u001b[94mCatalogPersistence\u001b[m (seam) exposes a minimal in"]
[0.000, "o", "terface (\u001b[94mload()\u001b[m, \u001b[94msave(CatalogSnapshot)\u001b[m, \u001b[94mwritePreImportBackup()\u001b[m)\r\n\u001b[6Cwith two adapters: \u001b[94mFileCatalogPersistence\u001b[m (atomic \u001b[94m.tmp\u001b[m write + rename and serialized write queue in iOS\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6CApplication Documents) and \u001b[94mInMemoryCatalogPersistence\u001b[m (for fast unit and widget tests).\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[94mLcscClient\u001b[39;1m seam\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • Single-method interface \u001b[94mFuture<LcscLookupResult> lookupPart(String lcscCode)\u001b[m that hides the \u001b[94mwmsc.lcsc.com\u001b[m URL\r\n\u001b[6Cconstruction, browser \u001b[94mUser-Agent\u001b[m header, \u001b[94mCx\u001b[5b\u001b[m normalization, HTML entity unescaping, and \u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m → \u001b[94mSpecs\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cmapping, backed by an\u001b[K\n\n\u001b[15D\u001b[90m.\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[11D\u001b[?2026l"]
