[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mDeep Module Seams & Adapters\u001b[m: Following \u001b[94mcodebase-design\u001b[m, we want a few deep modules with small interfaces\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommend yes\u001b[m: Use these exact three modules (\u001b[94mCatalogStore\u001b[m over \u001b[94mCatalogPersistence\u001b[m, \u001b[94mLcscClient\u001b[m, and pure\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mExternal Package Dependencies & Serialization\u001b[m: Should we lock the external dependency list in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkde8f20c8b49c7de5;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/pubspec.yaml\u0007pubspec.yaml\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\u001b[24Dn \u001b[94mbuild_run\u001b[m\r\n\n\n\n\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mDeep Module Seams & Adapters\u001b[m: Following \u001b[94mcodebase-design\u001b[m, we want a few deep modules with small interfaces\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommend yes\u001b[m: Use these exact three modules (\u001b[94mCatalogStore\u001b[m over \u001b[94mCatalogPersistence\u001b[m, \u001b[94mLcscClient\u001b[m, and pure\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mExternal Package Dependencies & Serialization\u001b[m: Should we lock the external dependency list in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk1239504009548987;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/pubspec.yaml\u0007pubspec.yaml\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\u001b[13D\u001b[94mner\u001b[m code ge\r\n\n\n\n\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mDeep Module Seams & Adapters\u001b[m: Following \u001b[94mcodebase-design\u001b[m, we want a few deep modules with small interfaces\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  placed at real seams (where production and test adapters actually vary) rather than shallow pass-through layers.\r\n  Should we structure \u001b[94mlib/\u001b[m around these three module seams?\r\n\n  1. \u001b[94mCatalogStore\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mCatalogPersistence\u001b[39;1m seam\u001b[m:\n\u001b[38D• \u001b[94mCatalogStore\u001b[m (deep module) owns all domain rules: 1-to-1 \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m uniqueness, duplicate \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cwarning lookup, stock clamping (\u001b[94m>= 0\u001b[m), container deletion cascading (\u001b[94mcontainerId: null, slot: null\u001b[m), and pre-\r\n\u001b[6Cimport validation.\n\u001b[18D• \u001b[94mCatalogPersistence\u001b[m (seam) exposes a minimal interface (\u001b[94mload()\u001b[m, \u001b[94msave(CatalogSnapshot)\u001b[m, \u001b[94mwritePreImportBackup()\u001b[m)\r\n\u001b[6Cwith two adapters: \u001b[94mFileCatalogPersistence\u001b[m (atomic \u001b[94m.tmp\u001b[m write + rename and serialized write queue in iOS\r\n\u001b[6CApplication Documents) "]
[0.000, "o", "and \u001b[94mInMemoryCatalogPersistence\u001b[m (for fast unit and widget tests).\r\n  2. \u001b[94mLcscClient\u001b[39;1m seam\u001b[m:\n\u001b[15D• Single-method interface \u001b[94mFuture<LcscLookupResult> lookupPart(String lcscCode)\u001b[m that hides the \u001b[94mwmsc.lcsc.com\u001b[m URL\r\n\u001b[6Cconstruction, browser \u001b[94mUser-Agent\u001b[m header, \u001b[94mCx\u001b[5b\u001b[m normalization, HTML entity unescaping, and \u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m → \u001b[94mSpecs\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cmapping, backed by an injectable \u001b[94mhttp.Client\u001b[m (or fake adapter in tests).\r\n  3. \u001b[94mPartSearchEngine\u001b[39;1m (pure module, no adapter needed)\u001b[m:\n\u001b[49D• Stateless function/class taking \u001b[94m(parts, containers, SearchQuery)\u001b[m and returning ranked/grouped results—hiding\r\n\u001b[6CUnicode symbol folding (\u001b[94mµ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mu\u001b[m, \u001b[94mΩ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mr\u001b[m), SI/EE-infix engineering unit parsing (\u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m, \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m0.1uF\u001b[m), 10-field\r\n\u001b[6Cmulti-token \u001b[94mAND\u001b[m matching, 3-tier relevance ranking, and natural alphanumeric \u001b[94mSlot\u001b[m sorting.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommend yes\u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "m: Use these exact three modules (\u001b[94mCatalogStore\u001b[m over \u001b[94mCatalogPersistence\u001b[m, \u001b[94mLcscClient\u001b[m, and pure\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\r\n  \u001b[94mPartSearchEngine\u001b[m), avoiding shallow repository/use-case pass-through layers.\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[1m## ❓ Q3 - External Package Dependencies & Serialization: Should we lock the external dependency list in           \u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[34;1;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd9dfc0b705f973c9;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/pubspec.yaml\u0007p\u001b[22mubspec.yaml\u001b[39;24;1m\u001b]8;;\u0007 to the following minimal set, using hand-written \u001b[94mfromJson\u001b[39m/\u001b[94mtoJson\u001b[39m (\u001b[94mdart:convert\u001b[39m) rather than \u001b[10b\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94;1mbuild_runner\u001b[39m code generation?\u001b[m\r\n⣽  \u001b[90mGenerating...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: View and review artifacts with /artifact.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "───────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[84X\u001b[84C\u001b[2mGemini 4 Argon · medium\u001b[m\r\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
