[0.008, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\n\n\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[31A\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> /to-tickets\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 25s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  Here is the proposed breakdown of \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkaa4dfacb79eff6f4;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/.scratch/parts-tracker-v1/spec.md\u0007spec.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 into \u001b[1m5 tracer-bullet vertical slices\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mCore Part catalog tracer bullet (JSON persistence, Workbench accordion list, stock adjustments, and manual\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mAdd/Edit Part)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n      • \u001b[1mBlocked by\u001b[m: None (can start immediately)\r\n\t\u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end runnable app with \u001b[94m@freezed\u001b[m models (\u001b[94mPart\u001b[m, \u001b[94mContainer\u001b[m, \u001b[94mCatalogSnapshot\u001b[m), \u001b[94m@riverpod\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mCatalog\u001b[m state, atomic persistence to \u001b[94mparts_catalog.json\u001b[m (plus iOS \u001b[94mInfo.plist\u001b[m Files app sharing keys), and the\u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "K\r\n\u001b[6CDark Command Bar & Inline Accordion workbench UI. Users can browse \u001b[1mParts\u001b[m, expand a card inline to view \u001b[1mSpecs\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6Cchips and adjust stock (\u001b[94m-10\u001b[m, \u001b[94m-1\u001b[m, \u001b[94m+1\u001b[m, \u001b[94m+10\u001b[m), open the \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m Detail sheet (\u001b[94mSet…\u001b[m exact quantity, open PDF\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mdatasheetUrl\u001b[m via \u001b[94murl_launcher\u001b[m, edit/delete), and manually add or edit \u001b[1mParts\u001b[m and their \u001b[94mKey: Value\u001b[m \u001b[1mSpecs\u001b[m.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mPhysical storage hierarchy (\u001b[94;22mContainer\u001b[39;1m management, 1-to-1 \u001b[94;22mSlot\u001b[39;1m uniqueness, and \u001b[94;22mBy Container\u001b[39;1m grouped view)\u001b[m\r\n      • \u001b[1mBlocked by\u001b[m: Ticket 1\u001b[K\r\n\t\u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end physical storage organization. Users can create, rename, edit descriptions for,\r\n\u001b[6Cand delete \u001b[1mContainers\u001b[m in the Manage Containers sheet (showing assigned \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m counts and atomically unassigning\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mParts\u001b[m on container deletion), assign a \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m to a \u001b[1mContainer\u001b[m and on-the-fly \u001b[1mSlot\u001b[m with strict 1-to-1 "]
