[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[28A      • \u001b[1mBlocked by\u001b[m: Ticket 1\u001b[K\r\n      • \u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end LCSC integration in the Add/Edit \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m sheet. Entering a \u001b[94mCxxxxxx\u001b[m code and tapping\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[6C\u001b[1mFetch LCSC\u001b[m queries \u001b[94mwmsc.lcsc.com/ftps/wm/product/detail\u001b[m via \u001b[94mLcscClient\u001b[m, pre-filling editable fields (\u001b[94mname\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mmanufacturer\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m, \u001b[94mpackage\u001b[m, \u001b[94mdatasheetUrl\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mSpecs\u001b[m from \u001b[94mparamVOList\u001b[m) with graceful offline/manual\r\n\u001b[6Cfallback. Entering an \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m already present in the catalog displays an inline warning banner with a \u001b[1mJump to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mPart\u001b[m action.\r\n  4. \u001b[1mMulti-token catalog search, filter chips, and SI / EE-infix engineering unit equivalence\u001b[m\n\u001b[87D• \u001b[1mBlocked by\u001b[m: Ticket 2\n\u001b[22D• \u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end workbench search and facet filtering (\u001b[94mPartSearchEngine\u001b[m). Searching runs multi-\r\n\u001b[6Ctoken \u001b[94mAND\u001b[m matching across all 10 \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m fields (\u001b[94mname"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmanufacturer\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m, \u001b[94mpackage\u001b[m, \u001b[94mContainer.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mname\u001b[m, \u001b[94mslot\u001b[m, \u001b[94mnotes\u001b[m, \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m) with Unicode folding (\u001b[94mµ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mu\u001b[m, \u001b[94mΩ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mr\u001b[m), SI and EE-infix value equivalence (\u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m ↔\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m4700R\u001b[m, \u001b[94m0.1uF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m10\u001b[4bpF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m3v3\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m, without bare 3-digit EIA expansion), and 3-tier relevance ranking.\r\n\u001b[6CUsers can filter via \u001b[94mAll\u001b[m, \u001b[94mLow Stock\u001b[m, \u001b[94mUnassigned\u001b[m, and dynamic category \u001b[94mChoiceChip\u001b[ms (intersecting via \u001b[94mAND\u001b[m with\r\n\u001b[6Csearch and hiding empty \u001b[1mContainers\u001b[m in \u001b[94mBy Container\u001b[m mode when filtered).\r\n  5. \u001b[1miOS Share Sheet backup export and validated full-snapshot JSON import\u001b[m\n\u001b[68D• \u001b[1mBlocked by\u001b[m: Ticket 2\n\u001b[22D• \u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end backup and restore. Users can trigger \u001b[1mExport Backup\u001b[m to share a timestamped\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mparts-catalog-YYYY-MM-DD.json\u001b[m f"]
[0.000, "o", "ile via the iOS Share Sheet (\u001b[94mshare_plus\u001b[m), or \u001b[1mImport Backup\u001b[m (\u001b[94mfile_picker\u001b[m) to\r\n\u001b[6Cvalidate an incoming JSON snapshot (\u001b[94mschemaVersion == 1\u001b[m, required fields, \u001b[94mquantity >= 0\u001b[m, no duplicate IDs, valid\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mcontainerId\u001b[m references, and 1-to-1 \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m uniqueness), confirm replacement against a summary of\r\n\u001b[6Ccurrent vs. incoming counts and \u001b[94mupdatedAt\u001b[m timestamps, write \u001b[94mparts_catalog.backup.json\u001b[m, and replace the live\r\n\u001b[6Ccatalog.\r\n\n  ──────\r\n  Does this granularity and dependency graph (\u001b[94m1 → {2, 3}\u001b[m and \u001b[94m2 → {4, 5}\u001b[m) feel right, or should any tickets be merged\r\n  or split before I publish them?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> lgtm\u001b[m\r\n⣻  \u001b[94mLoad\u001b[90ming...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────"]
