[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[29A\u001b[33;1mCreate file\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1m/Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/.scratch/parts-tracker-v1/issues/02-physical-storage-h\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 1 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m# 02: Physical storage hierarchy (Container management, 1-to-1 Slot uniqueness, and By Container grouped view)\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 2 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 3 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m**What to build:** End-to-end physical workbench storage organization using the fixed two-level \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Container →\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;1"]
[0.000, "o", "23mSlot`\u001b[39m hierarchy. Users can open the **Manage Containers** sheet from the command bar to view **Containers**\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mwith their assigned **Part** counts and create, rename, edit descriptions for, or delete **Containers**\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39m(atomically unassigning any **Parts** inside a deleted **Container**). In the Add / Edit **Part** sheet, users\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mcan assign a **Part** to \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Unassigned (Loose / Inbox)`\u001b[39m, to a bulk **Container** without a **Slot**, or to a\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mspecific \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`(Container, Slot)`\u001b[39m pair with strict 1-to-1 uniqueness validation. On the Workbench screen, users can\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mtoggle the **\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`By Container`\u001b[39m** chip to switch between the flat catalog list and a grouped view that pins\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m "]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Unassigned (Loose / Inbox)`\u001b[39m at the top, orders **Containers** alphabetically, sorts **Parts** inside each\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39m**Container** by natural alphanumeric **Slot** order (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`\"Page 2\"`\u001b[39m before \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`\"Page 10\"`\u001b[39m), and lets users tap **\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`+\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;123mAdd Slot`\u001b[39m** on any **Container** header to add a **Part** pre-assigned to that **Container**.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 4 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 5 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m**Blocked by:** 01: Core Part catalog tracer bullet (JSON persistence, Workbench accordion list, stock\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39madjustments, and manual Add/Edit Part)\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 6 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 7 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m**Status:** ready-for-agent\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 8 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 9 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m- [ ] The **Manage Containers** bottom sheet lists all **Containers** with their descriptions and assigned\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39m**Part** counts, and allows creating, renaming, editing descriptions for, and deleting **Containers**.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m  … 7 more lines (f for full diff)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[1mAllow creation of this file?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, allow creation\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. No, deny creation\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mf\u001b[90;22m full diff\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
[3.584, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\u001b[30A\u001b[35D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end workbench search and facet filtering (\u001b[94mPartSearchEngine\u001b[m). Searching runs multi-\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K token \u001b[94mAND\u001b[m matching across all 10 \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m fields (\u001b[94mname\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmanufacturer\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m, \u001b[94mpackage\u001b[m, \u001b[94mContainer.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mname\u001b[m, \u001b[94mslot\u001b[m, \u001b[94mnotes\u001b[m, \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m) with Unicode folding (\u001b[94mµ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mu\u001b[m, \u001b[94mΩ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mr\u001b[m), SI and EE-infix value equivalence (\u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m ↔\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K \u001b[94m4700R\u001b[m, \u001b[94m0.1uF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m10\u001b[4bpF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m3v3\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m, without bare 3-digit EIA expansion), and 3-tier relevance ranking.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K Users can filter via \u001b[94mAll\u001b[m, \u001b[94mLow Stock\u001b[m, \u001b[94mUnassigned\u001b[m, and dynamic category \u001b[94mChoiceChip\u001b[ms (intersecting via \u001b[94mAND\u001b[m with\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K search and hiding empty \u001b[1mContainers\u001b[m in \u001b[94mBy Container\u001b[m mode when filtered).\u001b[K\r\n  5. \u001b[1miOS Share Sheet bac"]
[0.000, "o", "kup export and validated full-snapshot JSON import\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[69D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mBlocked by\u001b[m: Ticket 2\u001b[K\n\u001b[23D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end backup and restore. Users can trigger \u001b[1mExport Backup\u001b[m to share a timestamped\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K \u001b[94mparts-catalog-YYYY-MM-DD.json\u001b[m file via the iOS Share Sheet (\u001b[94mshare_plus\u001b[m), or \u001b[1mImport Backup\u001b[m (\u001b[94mfile_picker\u001b[m) to\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K validate an incoming JSON snapshot (\u001b[94mschemaVersion == 1\u001b[m, required fields, \u001b[94mquantity >= 0\u001b[m, no duplicate IDs, valid\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K \u001b[94mcontainerId\u001b[m references, and 1-to-1 \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m uniqueness), confirm replacement against a summary of\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K current vs. incoming counts and \u001b[94mupdatedAt\u001b[m timestamps, write \u001b[94mparts_catalog.backup.json\u001b[m, and replace the live\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K catalog.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  Does this granularity and dependency graph (\u001b[94m1 → {2, 3}\u001b[m and \u001b[94m2 → {4, 5}\u001b[m) feel right, or should any tickets be merged\u001b[K\r\n  or split before I publish t"]
