[3.350, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\n\u001b[J\u001b[31A\u001b[6C• \u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end workbench search and facet filtering (\u001b[94mPartSearchEngine\u001b[m). Searching runs multi-\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K token \u001b[94mAND\u001b[m matching across all 10 \u001b[1mPart\u001b[m fields (\u001b[94mname\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlcscCode\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmpn\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmanufacturer\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m, \u001b[94mpackage\u001b[m, \u001b[94mContainer.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K \u001b[94mname\u001b[m, \u001b[94mslot\u001b[m, \u001b[94mnotes\u001b[m, \u001b[94mspecs\u001b[m) with Unicode folding (\u001b[94mµ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mu\u001b[m, \u001b[94mΩ\u001b[m→\u001b[94mr\u001b[m), SI and EE-infix value equivalence (\u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m ↔\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m4700R\u001b[m, \u001b[94m0.1uF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m10\u001b[4bpF\u001b[m, \u001b[94m3v3\u001b[m ↔ \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m, without bare 3-digit EIA expansion), and 3-tier relevance ranking.\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K Users can filter via \u001b[94mAll\u001b[m, \u001b[94mLow Stock\u001b[m, \u001b[94mUnassigned\u001b[m, and dynamic category \u001b[94mChoiceChip\u001b[ms (intersecting via \u001b[94mAND\u001b[m with\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K search and hiding empty \u001b[1mContainers\u001b[m in \u001b[94mBy Container\u001b[m mode when filtered).\u001b[K\r\n  5. \u001b[1miOS Share Sheet backup "]
[0.000, "o", "export and validated full-snapshot JSON import\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[69D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mBlocked by\u001b[m: Ticket 2\u001b[K\n\u001b[23D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: End-to-end backup and restore. Users can trigger \u001b[1mExport Backup\u001b[m to share a timestamped\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K \u001b[94mparts-catalog-YYYY-MM-DD.json\u001b[m file via the iOS Share Sheet (\u001b[94mshare_plus\u001b[m), or \u001b[1mImport Backup\u001b[m (\u001b[94mfile_picker\u001b[m) to\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K validate an incoming JSON snapshot (\u001b[94mschemaVersion == 1\u001b[m, required fields, \u001b[94mquantity >= 0\u001b[m, no duplicate IDs, valid\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K \u001b[94mcontainerId\u001b[m references, and 1-to-1 \u001b[94m(Container, Slot)\u001b[m uniqueness), confirm replacement against a summary of\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K current vs. incoming counts and \u001b[94mupdatedAt\u001b[m timestamps, write \u001b[94mparts_catalog.backup.json\u001b[m, and replace the live\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K catalog.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  Does this granularity and dependency graph (\u001b[94m1 → {2, 3}\u001b[m and \u001b[94m2 → {4, 5}\u001b[m) feel right, or should any tickets be merged\u001b[K\r\n  or split before I publish them?"]
