[0.000, "o", "leting **Containers**.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 4 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m- [ ] Deleting a **Container** prompts for confirmation showing how many **Parts** are inside it and atomically\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39munassigns those **Parts** (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`containerId: null, slot: null`\u001b[39m) in the same state and persistence update.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 5 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m- [ ] In the Add / Edit **Part** sheet, users can select \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Unassigned (Loose / Inbox)`\u001b[39m or any existing\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39m**Container** from a dropdown and enter an optional on-the-fly **Slot** string label (if \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`containerId`\u001b[39m is\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`null`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`slot`\u001b[39m is cleared to \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`null`\u001b[39m).\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 6 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m- [ ] Assigning a **Part** to a non-empty \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`(Container, Slot)`\u001b[39m p"]
