[0.084, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[29A\u001b[33;1mPending edit\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1m/Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_skilled/.scratch/parts-tracker-v1/issues/05-backup-export-and-\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m1 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m**Status:** ready-for-agent\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m1 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m**Status:** completed\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m2 \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m3 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m- [ ] Triggering **Export Backup** from the command bar writes the current \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`CatalogSnapshot`\u001b[39m (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`schemaVersion:\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m1`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;"]
[0.000, "o", "123m`updatedAt`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`containers`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`parts`\u001b[39m) as 2-space pretty-printed JSON to a timestamped\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`parts-catalog-YYYY-MM-DD.json`\u001b[39m file and opens the iOS Share Sheet.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m4 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m- [ ] Triggering **Import Backup** opens the system file picker for \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`.json`\u001b[39m files and runs strict all-or-nothing\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39mvalidation on the selected file before modifying any state.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m5 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m- [ ] Import validation rejects files with malformed JSON, unsupported \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`schemaVersion`\u001b[39m (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`!= 1`\u001b[39m), missing\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39mrequired fields (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`id`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`name`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`quantity >= 0`\u001b[39m), duplicate \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Container.id`\u001b[39m or \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Part.id`\u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "39m values, any\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Part.containerId`\u001b[39m that does not exist in \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`containers`\u001b[39m, or duplicate non-empty \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`(containerId, slot)`\u001b[39m pairs\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39m(case-insensitive after trimming).\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m6 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m- [ ] When an imported file fails validation, the app displays a clear, non-destructive error dialog explaining\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39mthe validation failure and leaves the existing catalog and \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`parts_catalog.json`\u001b[39m untouched.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m7 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m- [ ] When an imported file passes validation, the app presents a confirmation dialog showing current vs.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39mincoming **Part** counts, **Container** counts, and \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`updatedAt`\u001b[39m timestamps before replacing the catalog.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m8 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31"]
